  "patterns": [
    {
      "id": "learn-at-school",
      "pattern": "[Verb] + فِي الـ[Place]",
      "exampleArabic": "أتعلم في الجامعة",
      "exampleTransliteration": "ataʿallamu fī l-jāmiʿati",
      "exampleEnglish": "I learn at the university.",
      "grammarNote": "تَعَلَّمَ ('to learn') is Form V (تَفَعَّلَ) — built directly from Form II عَلَّمَ (level 54, 'to teach') by adding a تَـ prefix: عَلَّمَ → تَعَلَّمَ, a real and common relationship ('cause to know' → 'come to know for oneself'). Unlike Forms II/III/IV, whose present-tense prefix takes damma, Forms V and beyond take FATHA: أَتَعَلَّمُ, تَتَعَلَّمُ, تَتَعَلَّمِينَ, يَتَعَلَّمُ, نَتَعَلَّمُ — because the تَـ is now part of the stem itself, not a separate present-tense marker. Even without diacritics, تَتَعَلَّمُ ('you learn/she learns') and تُعَلِّمُ (level 54, 'you teach/she teaches') stay visually distinct: تتعلم vs. تعلم — the extra ت from Form V's prefix is a real letter, not a diacritic, so it survives the fade.",
      "audio": { "id": "phrase_ataallamu_fi_aljaamiaa", "text": "أتعلم في الجامعة" },
      "introducedInLevel": 62
    }
  ],
